{"type": "result", "session_id": "20260930_162133_074b36", "exit_code": 0, "text": "# The 14-Inch Workhorse: Run AI Models on Your Desk, Not in the Cloud\n\nIT Directors, here\u2019s a new option for your mid-size engineering shops: a 14-inch mobile workstation that handles open-weight language models and professional graphics workloads locally. It\u2019s built for teams that need to ship faster without relying on external servers or cloud subscriptions.\n\n## Local AI Without Compromise\n\nEngineers can run open-weight language models up to about 30 billion parameters directly on the device in configurations with 64 GB of memory or more. This is enabled by the Helix H9 AI processor, which includes 16 cores and an integrated NPU rated at 60 TOPS. Data scientists gain the ability to prototype and test locally without waiting for cloud resources or managing external infrastructure.\n\n## Professional Graphics in a Portable Form\n\nDesigners and engineers working with complex 3D models or video can leverage the Vireo V8000 Pro discrete GPU with 16 GB of dedicated graphics memory. The 14-inch OLED display matches professional standards with 2880 \u00d7 1800 resolution, 120 Hz refresh rate, and 100% DCI-P3 color gamut. This allows teams to review color-critical work and render scenes without sending assets back to a desktop or rendering farm.\n\n## Built for the Enterprise\n\nThe machine ships with Windows 11 Pro and includes security features such as a fingerprint reader, IR camera, TPM 2.0, and self-healing BIOS. IT teams can plan for predictable maintenance with a 3-year on-site, next-business-day service standard, extendable to 5 years. The chassis weighs starting at 1.65 kg (3.64 lb), making it easy for field engineers and consultants to carry between offices and client sites.\n\nMemory is user-upgradeable to 128 GB across two SO-DIMM slots, and storage can be expanded to 4 TB via two M.2 slots. Ports include 2 \u00d7 Thunderbolt 5, 1 \u00d7 USB-A 3.2, 1 \u00d7 HDMI 2.1, an SD card reader, and a 3.5 mm headphone jack. The 86 Wh battery delivers up to 11 hours of local video playback, allowing users to work away from power outlets for full workdays.\n\n## Why Consider This for Your Engineering Teams?\n\nMid-size engineering firms often struggle to balance the need for high-performance computing with the constraints of portability and budget. Many teams currently rely on desktop workstations for AI and graphics tasks, which means engineers cannot bring their full environment to client sites or meetings. With the Aurora 14 AI Workstation, your team gains the ability to run complex models and graphics applications on a device that fits easily in a laptop bag.\n\nThe local processing capability also reduces latency and improves data privacy. Engineers can work with proprietary models and sensitive client data without sending it through external networks. For IT departments, the self-healing BIOS and extended warranty options reduce the burden of troubleshooting and on-site service calls.\n\n## Take Control of Your Engineering Workflow\n\nThis workstation is available from Q4 with a starting price of $2,899 for the base configuration. Contact us today to discuss how we can help your team equip for local AI processing and professional graphics workflows. Let\u2019s build a solution that gives your engineers the tools they need to innovate, wherever they work.", "tokens": {"input": 565, "output": 720, "total": 5104, "cache_read": 3819, "cache_write": 0}, "duration_ms": 79567, "timestamp": 1790810573365}